ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 398 Tm
(Guardian Shell has the right product shape for LLM-agent governance, but its security) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 383 Tm
(core still needs to evolve toward stronger identity and stronger enforcement locality.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 358 Tm
(The most important engineering decisions are:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 333 Tm
(1. make cgroup-backed session identity primary) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 312 Tm
(2. move file and exec decisions deeper into LSM-first logic) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 291 Tm
(3. add seccomp as standard hardening) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 270 Tm
(4. isolate policy per session) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 249 Tm
(5. preserve the current rich observability and approval plane) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 228 Tm
(If those changes are made, the architecture will be substantially better aligned with) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 213 Tm
(the actual LLM-agent threat model.) Tj
